@page "/render/wasm"
@rendermode InteractiveWebAssembly

<PageTitle>InteractiveWebAssembly Render Mode</PageTitle>

<h1>InteractiveWebAssembly Render Mode</h1>

<p>
    This page uses <code>@@rendermode InteractiveWebAssembly</code>. The component is loaded as a WebAssembly app in the browser
    and runs entirely on the client after initial download.
</p>

<p>
    <strong>Why this mode is chosen:</strong>
    Choose <code>InteractiveWebAssembly</code> when you need client-side performance, offline capability, or reduced server load after the app is downloaded.
    It is the best choice for feature-rich client experiences and apps that must remain responsive without constant server interaction.
</p>

<p>
    <strong>Best cases:</strong>
    line-of-business apps with heavy UI interactions, offline-enabled workflows, and apps deployed to edge locations where client execution is preferred.
</p>

